{
 "_doc": [
  "World sea zones for tools/regions_world.py (milestone M1 'world ocean').",
  "Polygons are lon/lat rings with lon in [-169, 191] (the map seam is 169 W; 191 = 169 W seen from the east edge).",
  "A sea piece outside vanilla Europe takes the FIRST zone in this list whose polygon holds it (so small seas come",
  "before oceans); pieces in no polygon take the nearest zone. Water not connected to the ocean (lakes, Caspian) is",
  "filler land, matching the pathfinding grid (world sea = the largest water body). A key starting with 'eur_' extends that",
  "vanilla region. 'reuse' is the existing vanilla key used instead in the no-new-keys variant (regions_reuse.esf)."
